 "level_lemma": {
  "statement": "If G is (k-1)-colourable and u,v are non-adjacent, then G has proper k-colourings with colour(u)=colour(v) and with colour(u)!=colour(v); hence relation(u,v,k) is 'free'.",
  "proof": "Equal: (k-1)-colour G-{u,v} and give u and v a fresh k-th colour. Different: (k-1)-colour G; if u,v differ, done, otherwise recolour v with the unused k-th colour.",
  "consequence": "A level-5 virtual edge must be non-4-colourable, i.e. chi >= 5. The smallest known 5-chromatic unit-distance graph has 509 vertices (Parts 2020).",
  "seed_application": "The chosen seed is 3-colourable, so relation(u,v,5) is necessarily 'free'. Every 4-colourable supergraph is 'free' by the same lemma, so success requires a 5-chromatic extension."
 },
