 "conclusion": "NEGATIVE_TARGETED: 400 unit-circle growth candidates containing the seed (max n reached 40) never forced u != v at k=5; relation histogram {'free': 400}. The seed itself is 3-colourable (n=8, m=11) with relation 'free' at k=4 and k=5; all 32 sqrt(3)-edge seeds are 3-colourable. By the level lemma a level-5 virtual edge must be 5-chromatic, and no 5-chromatic unit-distance graph with fewer than 509 vertices is known. The seed therefore cannot be a partial gadget: the missing ingredient is a 5-chromatic unit-distance graph, which is the full open problem, not a local extension. The long chain does show a 40-vertex unit-distance supergraph of the seed that is 3-colourable, so size alone is not the obstruction -- chromatic structure is.",
